    "title": "2026 World Baseball Classic: How to watch the USA vs. Dominican Republic semifinal game tonight, where to stream and more",
    "text": "Team USA has advanced past the quarterfinals at the World Baseball Classic and will now face the Dominican Republic in the semifinals this Sunday. The USA vs. Dominican Republic semifinal game will air on Fox and FOX Deportes tonight at 8 p.m. ET. The game will also stream on FOX One. Here's everything you need to know about how to watch the 2026 World Baseball Classic, including the full schedule and where to watch.Date: Sunday, March 15AdvertisementTime: 8 p.m. ETChannels: Fox, Fox DeportesStreaming: FOX One, DirecTV, Fubo & moreUSA vs. Dominican Republic semifinal game time: The Dominican Republic vs. USA game at the World Baseball Classic will take place tonight, March 15, at 8 p.m. ET.USA vs. Dominican Republic semifinal game channel:The USA vs. Dominican Republic game will be broadcast live on Fox and in Spanish on FOX Deportes.Where to watch the World Baseball Classic without cableEvery single World Baseball Classic game will stream on FOX One. You can also catch games that are broadcast on Fox, FS1 and FS2 on platforms like DirecTV and Fubo.FOX One is a new streaming service from FOX that launched in 2025. With a subscription to FOX One, you can tune in to all your favorite FOX channels like FOX News, FOX Sports, FOX Weather, FS1, FS2, FOX Business, FOX Deportes, Big Ten Network (B1G), and local FOX stations all in one place, and this year, they'll be streaming every single game of the 2026 World Baseball Classic. FOX One offers live programming, as well as shows and movies on demand. The base price for FOX One will cost $19.99 a month, or you can save with an annual subscription for $199.99. World Baseball Classic ScheduleSunday, March 15, 2026United States @ Dominican Republic: 8:00 PM ET (FOX, FS1)Monday, March 16, 2026Venezuela @ Italy: 8:00 PM ET (FS1)Tuesday, March 17, 2026TBD @ TBD: 8:00 PM ET (FOX)",
